Package: directadjust
Title: Data-Driven Adjustment for Multiple Treatments
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sara", "LaPlante", role = "aut"),
    person("Sofia", "Triantafillou", role = "aut"),
    person("Emilija", "Perkovic", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "perkovic@uw.edu"))
Description: Certifies valid covariate adjustment sets for two treatments
    directly from conditional independence tests, without learning a causal
    graph as an intermediate object. Implements the R1 Build and R1 Combine
    procedures (Theorems 5 and 7 of LaPlante, Triantafillou and Perkovic,
    "Data-Driven Adjustment for Multiple Treatments", Journal of Causal
    Inference), together with a joint-effect estimator over the certified
    sets. The paper's simulation study ships under inst/simulation, with its
    saved results under inst/results.
